0..76 Comment "// A returner\'s row may stay open through a row variable, an implicit of the"
77..156 Comment "// kind `Row`: `log` prints through `std.io.Console.Eff` and leaves the rest of"
157..232 Comment "// its row to its caller, so one definition is used under every row holding"
233..317 Comment "// `std.io.Console.Eff`, the variable solved at each call by the row equation, and a"
318..415 Comment "// handler of `std.io.Console.Eff` takes `[std.io.Console.Eff | r]` to `[r]`, forwarding the rest"
416..490 Comment "// (Hillerström and Lindley, \"Liberating Effects with Rows and Handlers\","
491..570 Comment "// Type-Driven Development 2016, § 2.5 and § 3.3, T-HANDLER). What refuses is"
571..625 Comment "// in `../../pathological/control/row-variable.gandr`."
626..628 Comment "//"
629..644 Comment "// - see: #2270"
646..678 Comment "// The console\'s host interface."
